From: Manchego Stars engine
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] Arena (#265): ArenaUi_Init selects optional campaign palette + chapter face

Install the campaign-agnostic Arena presentation seam at the real init call site.

Notes:

_patch_arena_presentation_text: Route ArenaUi_Init's palette and attendant through build-generated selectors.

Graphics and TSA stay on their vanilla symbols. The generated selectors carry explicit
vanilla fallbacks, so an unconfigured campaign remains byte-semantically vanilla here.
---
diff --git a/src/uiarena.c b/src/uiarena.c
index 1dc97807e7cd081df02064733fb80190d01887f5..3ded56b4d18db68f3a743f26060b7d641d46a03d 100644
--- a/src/uiarena.c
+++ b/src/uiarena.c
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@ extern struct ProcCmd gProcScr_ArenaUiResultBgm[];
 
 void StartArenaDialogue(int, ProcPtr);
 void DrawArenaOpponentDetailsText(ProcPtr);
+const u16 * GetArenaPresentationPalette(void);
+int GetArenaPresentationFace(void);
 
 //! FE8U = 0x080B5730
 s8 sub_80B5730(void) {
@@ -64,7 +66,7 @@ void ArenaUi_Init(ProcPtr proc) {
 
     InitTalk(0x200, 2, 0);
     ResetFaces();
-    StartTalkFace(0x67, 0x20, 8, 3, 1);
+    StartTalkFace(GetArenaPresentationFace(), 0x20, 8, 3, 1);
 
     Decompress(Tsa_ShopWindows, gGenericBuffer);
 
@@ -118,7 +120,7 @@ void ArenaUi_Init(ProcPtr proc) {
 
     Decompress(gGfx_ArenaBuildingFront, (void*)(GetBackgroundTileDataOffset(3) + VRAM));
     CallARM_FillTileRect(gBG3TilemapBuffer, gTsa_ArenaBuildingFront, 0xc000);
-    ApplyPalettes(gPal_ArenaBuildingFront, 0xC, 4);
+    ApplyPalettes(GetArenaPresentationPalette(), 0xC, 4);
 
     BG_EnableSyncByMask(8);
 
